# CODEOWNERS — anti-drift protection.
#
# Every path listed here requires Anushka's review before a PR can merge.
# The goal is to keep parallel work on other devices (agents or humans)
# from silently overwriting decisions, security wiring, or the schema
# without a human sign-off. Trivial paths (public/, docs/, brand/) are
# deliberately not listed so day-to-day PRs stay unblocked.
#
# For this file to actually enforce reviews, GitHub branch protection
# on `main` must be set to require review from Code Owners — see the
# branch-protection checklist in the PR that introduced this file.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/managing-repository-settings/about-code-owners

# The beating heart. Any change to the app bootstrap, session model,
# schema DDL, cron jobs, or top-level middleware runs through review.
/server.js                @anushkanavin-afk

# Core libraries — auth, crypto, migrations, native-push, admin-auth.
# A silent change here is the highest-blast-radius kind.
/lib/                     @anushkanavin-afk

# HTTP surface. Any new route, deleted route, or auth-wrapper change
# is a security-adjacent event.
/routes/                  @anushkanavin-afk

# Schema. Migrations are immutable-once-applied by convention; the
# CODEOWNERS rule adds a mechanical review on any change here so the
# convention has teeth.
/migrations/              @anushkanavin-afk

# Test suite. Regression fences (idor, migrations, entry-crypto,
# admin-auth, smoke) are the guardrails; edits go through review.
/test/                    @anushkanavin-afk

# Security artifacts — audit reports, threat models, key handling notes.
/security/                @anushkanavin-afk

# Ops scripts — backups, migrations, encryption backfill, storage audit.
/scripts/                 @anushkanavin-afk

# Deploy + config surface. Docker, Railway, dependency lockfile.
/Dockerfile*              @anushkanavin-afk
/railway.toml             @anushkanavin-afk
/package.json             @anushkanavin-afk
/package-lock.json        @anushkanavin-afk

# Repository governance — the anti-drift scaffolding itself.
/.github/                 @anushkanavin-afk
/CODEOWNERS               @anushkanavin-afk
/SECURITY.md              @anushkanavin-afk
